; Restores wpn_rpk74's icon, which renders as a garbled fragment in the
; inventory and the F7 debug spawner.
;
; MartinLore's Stalker 2 icons repoints the RPK family at the HD atlas
; ui\ui_stalker2_rifles by patching the parent section:
;
;   ![wpn_rpk]  icons_texture=ui\ui_stalker2_rifles  10x4 @ (52,12)  scale=2
;
; wpn_rpk74 inherits from wpn_rpk ([wpn_rpk74]:wpn_rpk in
; items/weapons/w_rpk.ltx, won by "410- 3DSS for GAMMA"), so it picks up the
; HD icons_texture and inv_grid_scale from the patched parent. But it also
; redeclares its own inv_grid_x/y/width/height, which are still the legacy
; ui_icon_equipment coordinates (5x2 @ 35,14). MartinLore patches
; wpn_rpk74_16 and wpn_rpk74_16_drum explicitly, but never plain wpn_rpk74,
; so nothing corrects them.
;
; The engine therefore samples a 250x100 window at (1750,700) out of the
; 4096x2048 HD atlas, a region belonging to unrelated weapons, and draws it
; in a ceil(5/2) x ceil(2/2) = 3x1 cell. That is the two disconnected pieces
; labelled "RPK-74" in the top-right of the debug spawner's By Icon panel.
;
; Fix: delete the four stale coordinates so the inheritance the override was
; silently breaking is restored. DLTX drops a "!key" line in the base+mods
; merge (IsMergingBaseAndMod, Xr_ini.cpp), so the parent's value survives the
; parent merge that follows. Whatever wpn_rpk resolves to is what wpn_rpk74
; draws.
;
; Deleting rather than reassigning is deliberate. Neither wpn_rpk nor
; wpn_rpk74 declares icons_texture or inv_grid_scale of its own; both reach
; wpn_rpk74 only by inheritance from MartinLore's ![wpn_rpk]. Writing them
; here was redundant with the icon pack installed and wrong without it:
; icons_texture forced the section onto an atlas that wasn't there, and
; inv_grid_scale leaked to wpn_rpk74_16_drum, the one other section that
; inherits wpn_rpk74 ([wpn_rpk74_16_drum]:wpn_rpk74, won by "461- GIMP").
; The drum redeclares its texture and all four coordinates but not the scale,
; so it took ours and drew its 250x100 icon in a 3x1 cell. wpn_rpk74_16 was
; unaffected because it inherits identity_immunities, not wpn_rpk74.
;
; With the icon pack installed this resolves to exactly what assigning the HD
; coordinates did: ui\ui_stalker2_rifles, 10x4 @ (52,12), scale 2, keeping the
; inventory footprint at 5x2 cells. Without it, wpn_rpk74 falls back to
; wpn_rpk's vanilla ui_icon_equipment icon (5x2 @ 35,18) instead of its own
; (35,14) - a near-identical gun, and nothing is garbled. A DLTX patch cannot
; be conditioned on another mod's presence, so that is the tradeoff.
;
; Filename sorts after mod_system_zzzzzzzzzzzzzzz_s2rifles.ltx so this
; override is applied last.

